  "goodToKnow": "Das Bundesverfassungsgericht (BVerfG) in Karlsruhe is Germany's Federal Constitutional Court. It checks whether laws comply with the Grundgesetz and can strike them down: ein Gesetz kippen. Its 16 judges are elected half by the Bundestag and half by the Bundesrat. It's one of the most trusted institutions in Germany, and Karlsruhe hat entschieden is a powerful phrase. At 24 letters, the word is a great example of German compounding: Bund + es + Verfassung + s + Gericht."
